ntoskrnl.exe!PsTerminateSystemThread         all  required  w2k-export; win98-precedent bt829.sys 4.10.2222 (NTOSKRNL.EXE!PsTerminateSystemThread, hint BB); NUSB USBPORT.SYS 5.00.2195.5652 (hint C2) (Appendix A row 113)
ntoskrnl.exe!ObReferenceObjectByHandle      all  required  w2k-export; win98-precedent ks.sys 4.10.2222 (NTOSKRNL.EXE!ObReferenceObjectByHandle, hint AA) (+11 other 98 SE) (Appendix A row 116). Called on NT only (IoIsWdmVersionAvailable(1, 0x10): Windows 2000 is WDM 1.10, Windows 98 1.00, ME 1.05): the stop waits on the thread object there and on an event on Windows 98, where that wait faulted (runs/run-26.md). A NULL object type: PsThreadType is a data import
ntoskrnl.exe!ObfDereferenceObject           all  required  w2k-export; win98-precedent hidclass.sys 4.10.2222 (NTOSKRNL.EXE!ObfDereferenceObject, hint AC) (+16 other 98 SE) (Appendix A row 34). The ObDereferenceObject macro; NT only, as above
ntoskrnl.exe!IoIsWdmVersionAvailable        all  required  w2k-export; win98-precedent ohci1394.sys 4.10.2222 (NTOSKRNL.EXE!IoIsWdmVersionAvailable, hint 51) (Appendix A row 40); NUSB USBPORT.SYS 5.00.2195.5652 (hint 55). Chooses the thread-stop wait: (1, 0x10) is TRUE from Windows 2000 (WDM 1.10) on and FALSE on 98 (1.00) and ME (1.05)
ntoskrnl.exe!ExQueueWorkItem                 all  required  w2k-export; win98-precedent uhcd.sys 4.10.2222 (NTOSKRNL.EXE!ExQueueWorkItem, hint 17) (+23 other 98 SE); ntkern-name. The power work item (hcd_power.c): a D0 resume or a system-IRP completion that arrives above PASSIVE_LEVEL

# --- DbgPrint: the log ring's DebugView sink (hcd_log.c, task 26-A.8) in    ---
# --- every flavour, emitted from the controller thread at PASSIVE_LEVEL      ---
# --- only, and the qemu flavour's live trace (xhci_dbg.c). AGENTS.md allows  ---
# --- no third site, and SITES holds the import to those two objects.        ---
ntoskrnl.exe!DbgPrint                        all  required  SITES=hcd_log.obj,xhci_dbg.obj the one emit site and the qemu trace; w2k-export; win98-precedent ks.sys 4.10.2222 (NTOSKRNL.EXE!DbgPrint, hint 1) (+1 other 98 SE); ntkern-name (design record 13 section 7.4)
# --- The qemu flavour's port-0xE9 mirror, never published ---
HAL.dll!WRITE_PORT_UCHAR                     qemu required  w2k-export; ntkern-name; MEASURED NOT LOADING on E460 Win98 SE metal (the miniport's allowlist on branch 1.2.0.0 has the record; design record 08). The qemu flavour is never published, so this row is what keeps the import out of every binary a user can install.


